      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-06-30_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>MARRIAGE A FAILURE?</head>
        <p>MARRIAGE A FAILURE?</p>
        <p>What a question to ask, but oow often could it be answered in the affirmative, the prirvipal cause being the improvidence of Furnishing on the Hire System. Since r.ur adrertisements have appeared pointing out the disadvantages we have re- ceived several le tem, agreeing with our denunciations of this pernicious sys•..em. Each Hire Agreement specifies that after the deposit is paid, so may weekly payments shall be made and that until the whole of the snm mentioned is paid the goods shall not become the property of the would-be pur- chaser, and that if any of the payments are negitoted to the exact time specified the goods may be forcibly taken away and the whole of the payments forfeited. County Court judges have denounced the sy tem, inasmuch as the vendor gets both money and goods. Again, the pri es charged are enormous, without any respect being paid to the quality, in many cases being worn out before they are paid for. To colt- kat this system. and open the eyes of the public, WOrsley's of " The Pantheon," Gayt horn, Manchester, the Largest Retailers of Second-band Furniture in the world, have detertnined to allow all respectable householders to have furniture at the ticketed marked cash price, a small percentage being charged for the conveirence of payment by the week, month, or quarter. On the fomth page of the "Examiner" we advertise a list of Bargains every week, any of which can be had and paid for by convenient intervals, the articles being delivered upon the first payment being made. Furniture from £5 to £1 000 may be arranged for in this way. To give an idea of the equity of our proposals we are prepared to supply for a working man a House of Furniture complete, thoroughly good and sobstantinl (every article warranted). price £2O cash down, not a penny less, or leer cent extra if credit is given, making £22. Full particulars sent on application.</p>
        <p>GREAT BARGAINS AT WORSLEY'S. ONE HUNDRED BEDROOM SUITES ON VIEW.</p>
        <p>The Marvel: This is a solid American walnut Bedroom Suite, beautifully finished, has an excellent Wardrobe. with plate-glass centre door, Dreksings-table, enclo,•ed with large drawers, the top fitted with large swing mirror and jewel drawers, Washstand. with Carrara marble slab and Minton tile back, with shaving glass, the bottom prettily enclosed with cupboard and drawers, Chairs. and Towel Rail com- plete; a very pretty suite. 'What price for this, £25 or £3O? No, only 9 guineas. Money returned if not satisfactory. Ten per cent extra if credit is given. W. H. WORSLEY, 'The Pantheon," anythorn, Manchester.</p>
        <p>See Advertisement On pig, 4.</p>
