        <p>Nov,. „lite t",,TS has vet been finally decided with refer- )l4Eirt„;' e legal vacancies,but in the hest informed ),-"lair,-111t is understood that Sir John Rigby will t-DoCn in his present post, thus necessitating the 1/04.„1 Qf an en] being appointed from outside NIP Gully,QC Ml' will be made a k 4„ - • .....r. • •. • •• eiti "fi there will in consequence be a vacancy !Ti ;tr,;(',l° of the extreme probability that Sir klarcourt will adhere to his intention to the end of the session, a quiet canvass is ',Ltit; going on in order to ascertain who is &amp;„-ZelY to be accepted as his successor. There 1,41 b 40.171'a 'no doubt that it will be either Mr. , rlll4,:.nnerMan or Mr. John Morley, and if it 0, IR true that the latter does not desire '5743' will be pretty clear for the War Secre-</p>
