        <p>LAWN TENNIS.</p>
        <p>TENNIS MATCH AT NEWTON.</p>
        <p>A match between Newton and Mr. F. E. Barlow's Farnworth team, was played at Newton on Saturday, when Mr. Barlow brought a very strong team of six gentlemen and fourladies. In the gentlemen's doubles Newton were beaten by the 3 events to o,tut the ladies, doubles were both won by Newton, Mrs. Parkes and Miss K. Sankey especially distinguishing themselves. In the gentlemen's singles Newton were more succeesful scoring .3 events to 3. In the ladies singles Newton again came to the fore, Mrs. Parkes and Miss K. Sankey again coming in for praise for the way in which they of their opponenents. Taking the games al- together Newton won by 8 events to Farnworth 7 events or 10 sets to Farnworth 17 sets. or /99 games to Farn- worth 177 games Afterwards mixed doubles were played, Newton losing all 4 games. core</p>
      </div>
