        <p>WIDNES TOWN COUNCIL.</p>
        <p>A special meeting of this Council was held on Friday afternoon, at the Town Hall, under the presidency of Alderman Wareing, for the purpose of considering a report by the surveyor upon the collapse of tbe Weston outfall sewer on Ditton Marsh. After this had been read, Alderman Sadler, chairman of the Highway Com- mittee, caoved: " That the surveyor be instructed to proceed with the works be considered to be necessary to repair the sewer."—Councillor Niel seconded.—Alder- man Sadler, in reply to questions said the collapse of the ' sewer was attributed to the foundpations;which had been made on quicksand, giving way. Tney proposed that ; the money required for the repair of the sewer should he borrowed.—The motion was carried unanimously.— Councillor Barlow moved, and Counciller Bullough seconded, a motion " that application be made to the Local Government Board for the powers to bozrow £1,500, the estimated cost of repairing the sewer,' which was carried. This was all the business.—Th Mayor (A!derman Gossage) was still prevented from presiding over the raefsting through indispolition,</p>
      </div>
