        <p>RUNCORN BOWLING CLUB.</p>
        <p>A TUSSLE WITH VERDIN PARK. On Wednesday afternoon teams representin , . 5- Runcorn and Verdin Park, Northwich, engaged 1! a return match on the green belonging to the Par* men at Northwich. The weather was beautifully fine, ' and the green was in capital condition. When these ' teams met a short sime ago at Runcorn it will be rernea?` ' bered that the victory rested with a win for Verdis Park as will he seen from the score. After the match. the players partook of an excellent tea provided by bir-. Thomas Taylor of the SpArtsman's Arms. Subsequently, , an impromptu concert took place, which was a source of diversion to all. Ills following are the respectivt: scores : RUNCORN. VEnDIN PARR'. W Wright 159-15, y BBeobhbai nmg ta 0. n. ............................... 125:::1- T Dean T Woods S Johnson l5-15 J Hooey .................. u • J Woods l5 T Taylor l4 ' H Grundy T Barton l5 G May 7 5 6 J Mutch 6-15 R Molyneaux ............15 J Sillitoe 6 J Storey R Briscoe l2— 7 J .. Ridgeway ............. J Stritch .................. 15 J Gronnds l— 2 W Lea l5-1Q P Deakin J Shaw</p>
